hadiths[57]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2123","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The Children of Israel were commanded to enter (the gate of Jerusalem) bowing and to say, ""We seek forgiveness for our sins; your sins will be forgiven."" But the Children of Israel acted against the command and entered the gate dragging themselves on their buttocks and saying, ""A grain in the ear"" (meaning: we want wheat)."
"2124","Abu Ishaq says: I heard from Sayyiduna Bara’ (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: When the Ansar would return after performing Hajj, they would not enter their houses through the door, but would climb over from the back (wall). One Ansari came and entered through the door, so people talked to him about this. Then this verse was revealed: ""It is not righteousness that you enter houses from the back, but righteousness is to fear Allah, and enter houses through their doors."
"2125","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that when this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): (Allah’s is whatever is in the heavens and whatever is in the earth...) meaning, “Whatever is in the heavens and the earth belongs to Allah. Whether you disclose what is in your hearts or conceal it, Allah will call you to account for it. Then He will forgive whom He wills and punish whom He wills, and Allah has power over all things,” this verse was very hard on the Companions. They came to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and sat down on their knees. Then they said, “O Messenger of Allah! (Previously) we were made responsible for acts such as prayer, fasting, jihad, and charity, which we had the strength to do, but now this verse has been revealed to you, and we do not have the strength for it.” The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Do you want to say what the people of the two books (the Jews and Christians) before you said (that is, they said), ‘We have heard and we disobey,’ that we have heard (the word of Allah and His Messenger) but we do not accept it? Rather, you should say, ‘We have heard and we obey. O our Lord, we seek Your forgiveness, and to You is our return.’” So the Companions said, “We have heard and we obey. We seek forgiveness for our sins, O our Lord! And to You is our return.” When the Companions began to recite this, it became easy for their tongues to recite it, so Allah revealed these verses: (The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him...) meaning, “The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has believed in what was sent down to him from his Lord, and the believers (have believed as well). All of them have believed in Allah, His angels, His books, and His messengers. (They all say) ‘We make no distinction between any of His messengers (we believe in all the messengers, not that we believe in some and not in others),’ and they said, ‘We have heard and we obey. O our Lord, we seek Your forgiveness, and to You is the return.’” When the Companions did this (that is, recited these verses and recited them sincerely), Allah abrogated the verse (Whether you disclose what is in your hearts...) and revealed the verse (Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity...) meaning, “Allah does not burden any soul beyond its capacity. For it is what it has earned, and against it is what it has earned. O our Lord, do not lay upon us a burden like that which You laid upon those before us.” So Allah said, “Yes.” “O our Lord, do not place upon us a burden greater than we have strength to bear.” So Allah said, “Yes.” “And pardon us, forgive us, have mercy on us. You are our Protector, so help us against the disbelieving people.” So Allah said, “Yes.”"
"2126","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: “It is Allah who has sent down to you the Book; in it are verses that are clear and precise (muhkam), they are the foundation of the Book, and others are ambiguous (mutashabih, i.e., allegorical or with hidden meanings). Then those in whose hearts is deviation follow that which is ambiguous, seeking discord and seeking its interpretation, but no one knows its interpretation except Allah. And those firm in knowledge say: ‘We believe in it; all of it is from our Lord.’ And none take heed except those of understanding.” Mother of the Believers says that (after reciting) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you see those who pursue ambiguous verses, then avoid them, for they are the ones whom Allah has named (in the Qur’an). (That is, there is deviation in their hearts, so the believers should avoid such people.)"
"2127","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that there were some hypocrites during the blessed era of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who would stay behind when you, peace and blessings be upon him, went out for battle, and they were pleased to remain at home behind the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. Then when you, peace and blessings be upon him, returned, they would make excuses to you, swear oaths, and wish that people would praise them for deeds they had not done. Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""Do not think of those who rejoice for what they have done, and love to be praised for what they did not do, as being safe from the punishment; for them is a painful punishment."
"2128","It is narrated from Humaid bin Abdur Rahman bin Awf that Marwan said to his doorkeeper Rafi‘, ""Go to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) and say: If every person among us who is pleased with what he has done and wants people to praise him for what he has not done were to be punished, then all of us would be punished (because this flaw exists in all of us)."" So Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""What concern do you have with this verse? This verse was revealed regarding the People of the Book."" Then Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) recited this verse ((wa idh akhadhallahu...)) to the end, and then recited the verse ((la tahsabanna alladhina...)). Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked the People of the Book about something, so they concealed it and instead told him something else. Then they left in such a state that they made the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) think that they had told him what he had asked, and they sought praise from him, and in their hearts they were pleased with what they had done (i.e., with concealing the real matter which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had asked them about). So Allah the Exalted says about them that they will be punished, and what is meant is the People of the Book."
"2129","Narrated from Sayyiduna Urwah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) about the statement of Allah, the Exalted: “If you fear that you will not be able to deal justly with the orphan girls, then marry those women who please you, two, three, or four.” She said: O my nephew! This verse refers to the orphan girl who is under the guardianship (i.e., upbringing, like a niece under her uncle’s care) and shares in his wealth (for example, in the uncle’s wealth). Then the guardian is attracted to her wealth and beauty and wishes to marry her, but does not deal justly with her regarding her dowry and does not give her as much dowry as others would be willing to give. So Allah, the Exalted, forbade marrying such girls except in the case when they act justly and are willing to give the full dowry. And they were commanded to marry other women who please them (instead of these orphans). Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: After this verse was revealed, people again asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about these girls, so Allah, the Exalted, revealed this verse: “They ask you concerning women. Say: Allah gives you a ruling about them, and what is recited to you in the Book concerning the orphan girls to whom you do not give what is prescribed for them and yet you desire to marry them.” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: What Allah, the Exalted, mentioned, “If you fear that you will not be able to deal justly with the orphans, then marry those women who please you (other than them),” and Umm al-Mu’minin (may Allah be pleased with her) said: In the other verse, Allah’s statement, “and you desire to marry them,” means that one of you does not intend to marry that orphan girl who is under your care and is deficient in wealth and beauty. Thus, they were forbidden to marry that orphan woman who is wealthy and beautiful except in the case when they act justly (i.e., give them their full dowry and wealth, etc.). (The meaning is that in the beginning, people used to marry those orphan girls who were under their care and were wealthy and beautiful, but they would be dishonest with their wealth and not give the full dowry. In this case, in the verse at the beginning of the Surah, they were forbidden to marry them, but when the Companions asked about marrying them if it was better for the girls themselves, Allah, the Exalted, revealed verse 127 of Surah An-Nisa, stating that marrying them with justice is permissible and the best course of action.)"
"2130","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) regarding this verse: ""Whoever is rich, let him abstain (and whoever is poor, let him eat according to what is reasonable for him),"" that this verse was revealed about the person who is the guardian of an orphan's wealth and manages and improves it. So if he is needy, he may eat from it according to what is customary (and if he is wealthy, he should not take anything)."
"2131","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Zaid bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out for the Battle of Uhud, and among those who were with him, some men turned back (they were hypocrites and were about three hundred). The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became divided into two groups regarding their case. Some said, ""We will kill them,"" and others said, ""No! We will not kill them."" Then Allah the Exalted revealed this verse: ""What is the matter with you that you are divided into two groups regarding the hypocrites?"
"2132","Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Jubair says that I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Can the repentance of one who deliberately kills a believer be accepted?"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""No."" I recited to him the verse from Surah Al-Furqan: ((And those who do not invoke...)) to the end, after which it says: ((Except for those who repent...)) (because from this it appears that after unjust killing, repentance is possible). Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""This verse is Makki and it has been abrogated by the verse which was revealed in Madinah: 'Whoever deliberately kills a believer, his recompense is Hell, wherein he will abide forever.'"
"2133","‘Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that some Muslims saw a man with a few goats. He said, “As-salamu Alaikum.” The Muslims seized him, killed him, and took the goats. Then this verse was revealed: “Do not say to the one who greets you with peace that you are not a believer (but only say Salam to save your life).” Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) recited (Salam) in this verse, and some have recited (Silm) (so the meaning would be: the one who approaches you with peace)."
"2134","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said’ about this verse: “And if a woman fears ill-treatment or aversion from her husband, there is no sin upon them if they make terms of settlement between them { کوئی بات طے کر کے } ...” She said that this verse was revealed about a woman who is with a man, but he no longer wishes to keep her with him much; however, the woman has children and intimacy with her husband, and she dislikes leaving her husband, so she gives up her right regarding herself. (That is, she relinquishes her conjugal right.)"
"2135","Tariq bin Shihab says that a Jew came to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""O Commander of the Faithful! There is a verse in your Book which you recite; if it had been revealed to us Jews, we would have taken that day as a festival."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked, ""Which verse?"" The Jew replied, ""Today I have perfected your religion for you, completed My favor upon you, and have chosen for you Islam as your religion."" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""I know the day on which this verse was revealed and the place where it was revealed. This verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) at the place of Arafat on a Friday (and that day was a combination of two festivals for the Muslims: one was Friday and the other was the Day of Arafah)."
"2136","´Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` when this verse was revealed: ""Those who believe and do not mix their belief with injustice (i.e., do not get involved in sin), for them is security and they are the rightly guided,"" it was very difficult for the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). They said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Who among us does not wrong himself (i.e., commit sin)?"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""This verse does not mean what you think. Rather, by 'injustice' is meant what Luqman (peace be upon him) said to his son: 'O my son! Do not associate anything with Allah; indeed, associating partners with Allah is a great injustice.'"" (Luqman: 13)"
"2137","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When three things appear, then at that time, faith will not benefit anyone who did not have faith before or did not do good deeds: first, the rising of the sun from the place where it sets; second, the emergence of the Dajjal; and third, the emergence of the beast of the earth."
"2138","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) one day said to his companions: ""Do you know where this sun goes?"" They said, ""Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) know best."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It keeps moving until it reaches its resting place under the Throne, where it falls down in prostration (the reality of this prostration is known only to Allah Almighty). Then it remains in that state until it is commanded: 'Rise and return to where you came from.' So it returns and emerges from its rising place. Then it keeps moving until it reaches its resting place under the Throne and prostrates. Then it remains in that state until it is told: 'Rise and return to where you came from.' It then emerges from its rising place again. And it continues in this way. One day it will move in the same manner and people will not notice any difference in its movement until it reaches its resting place under the Throne. At that time, it will be said to it: 'Rise and emerge from the west, from where you set.' So it will emerge from the west."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know when this will be? (i.e., the sun rising from the west) It will be at that time 'when no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or had not earned any good through its faith.'"
"2139","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that a woman (in the time of ignorance) used to perform Tawaf of the Ka'bah naked and would say: ""Who will give me a cloth so that I may cover my private parts with it?"" And she would say: ""Today all or some will be exposed, then whatever is exposed I will never make lawful (i.e., it has become forbidden forever)."" (This indecent custom was abolished by Islam.) Then this verse was revealed: ""Wear your clothes at every place of worship."
"2140","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: A caller will call out (to the people of Paradise): It has been decreed for you that you will remain healthy and never fall ill, and indeed you will live and never die, and indeed you will remain young and never grow old, and indeed you will remain in bliss and comfort and never face any distress. And this is the meaning of Allah Almighty’s saying: ""The people of Paradise will be called: This is your Paradise which you have inherited because of what you used to do."
"2141","´Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` Abu Jahl, the accursed, said: ""O Allah! If this Qur'an is true and from You, then rain down stones upon us from the sky, or bring upon us a painful punishment."" At that time, this verse was revealed: ""Allah will not punish them while you (O Prophet) are among them, and Allah will not punish them while they seek forgiveness. And what is (the matter) with them that Allah should not punish them while they prevent (people) from entering Masjid al-Haram...,"" until the end."
"2142","Saeed bin Jubair says: I said to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), ""Surah At-Tawbah?"" He said, ""Surah At-Tawbah?"" And he said, ""Rather, that Surah is the one that humiliates and exposes (the disbelievers and hypocrites). In this Surah, it kept being revealed: 'And among them,' 'And among them,' until the hypocrites thought that none would be left whose mention would not be made in this Surah."" I said, ""Surah Al-Anfal?"" He said, ""That Surah is about the Battle of Badr (in it are mentioned the rulings of war booty)."" I said, ""Surah Al-Hashr?"" He said, ""That was revealed about Banu Nadir."
"2143","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that’ a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have derived pleasure from a woman on the outskirts of Madinah, and I did everything except intercourse. Now I am present before you, so pass whatever judgment you wish regarding me.” Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Allah had concealed your sin; it would have been better if you had concealed it as well.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not reply to him. Then the man stood up and left. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent a person after him, called him back, and recited this verse: ((Indeed, good deeds erase...)) A man said, “O Messenger of Allah! Is this ruling specific to him?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “No, rather it is for everyone.”"
"2144","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in a field, and he was leaning on a stick, when he passed by a group of Jews. One of them said to another, “Ask him about the soul.” The other said, “What doubt do you have that you want to ask? Perhaps he will say something that you will dislike.” Then they said, “Ask.” So some of them got up and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and asked him about the soul. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent and did not answer. I thought that revelation was coming to him. He says: I remained standing in that place. When the revelation had been sent down, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: “They ask you about the soul. Say: The soul is of the command of my Lord, and you have not been given knowledge except a little.”"
"2145","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding this verse: “Those whom they call upon, they themselves seek means of access to their Lord,” that some people used to worship certain jinn. Those jinn became Muslims (and their worshippers did not know about it). And those people continued to worship them, then this verse was revealed: “Those whom they worship, they themselves seek means of access to their Lord.”"
"2146","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says about this verse: ""Do not recite your prayer too loudly, nor too quietly, but seek a way between,"" that it was revealed in Makkah Mukarramah at a time when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was hiding in a house due to fear. The incident is that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) led the companions in prayer, he would recite the Qur'an aloud. So when the polytheists heard the sound of the Noble Qur'an, they would abuse the Qur'an, the One who revealed it (i.e., Allah Almighty), and the one upon whom it was revealed (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him). Upon this, Allah Almighty said to His Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Do not recite (the Qur'an) in prayer so loudly"" that the polytheists can hear it, ""nor recite (the Qur'an) so quietly"" that your companions cannot hear it, ""but recite (the Qur'an) in a moderate voice,"" between low and loud."
"2147","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says regarding the statement of Allah Almighty: (And do not recite your prayer too loudly...) that this was revealed about supplication (i.e., do not supplicate in a very loud voice nor in a very low voice)."
"2148","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection, a big, fat man will come who, in the sight of Allah, will not be equal to the wing of a mosquito. Recite this verse: ""We shall not assign any weight for them on the Day of Resurrection."" (That is, the fatness, wealth, and riches of the world will be of no use on the Day of Resurrection; there, only deeds are required. This hadith proves the condemnation of obesity.)"
"2149","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: On the Day of Resurrection, death will be brought in the form of a white ram and it will be placed between Hell and Paradise. Then it will be said, ""O people of Paradise! Do you recognize this?"" They will raise their heads, look at it, and say, ""Yes! We recognize it, it is death."" Then it will be said, ""O people of Hell! Do you recognize this?"" They too will raise their heads, look at it, and say, ""Yes! We recognize it, it is death."" Then it will be ordered that the ram be slaughtered. Then it will be said, ""O people of Paradise! You will live forever and there will never be death for you, and O people of Hell! You too will live forever and there will never be death for you."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recited this verse: ""And warn them of the Day of Regret when the matter will be decided, and they are in heedlessness and do not believe."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) pointed towards the world with his hand (meaning, they are so engrossed in the world that they have no fear of the Day of Resurrection)."
"2150","Sayyiduna Khabbab (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I had a debt upon ‘As bin Wa’il. I went to him to collect it, but he said, “I will never give it to you until you turn away from Muhammad (peace be upon him) and his religion.” I said, “I will not turn away from Muhammad (peace be upon him) even if you die and are resurrected.” He said, “If I am resurrected after death, then I will pay your debt.” Then this verse was revealed: “Have you seen the one who disbelieves in Our verses and says, ‘I will surely be given wealth and children’? Has he looked into the unseen, or has he taken a covenant with Allah?...” to the end."
"2151","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood among us to deliver a sermon and said: O people! You will be gathered before Allah barefoot, uncircumcised, and naked, “just as We began the first creation, We shall repeat it.” This is Our promise, and surely We shall fulfill it. (104) Beware! Among all creation, Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will be the first to be clothed on the Day of Resurrection. And beware! Some people from my Ummah will be brought, then they will be turned towards the left (the side of the disbelievers). I will say: O my Lord! These are my followers. It will be said in reply: You do not know what innovations they introduced after you. Then I will say what the righteous servant (Isa, peace be upon him) said: “I was a witness over them while I remained among them. But when You took me up, You were the Watcher over them (and I had no knowledge of them), and You are Witness over all things (meaning Your knowledge encompasses everything). If You punish them, they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, surely You are the Mighty, the Wise.” (Al-Ma’idah: 117-118) Then it will be said to me: After you departed, these people turned back (i.e., they apostatized from the religion)."
"2152","Sayyiduna Qais bin ‘Abad says: I heard Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) swear (regarding this verse of Surah Al-Hajj) that: “Indeed, these two groups are enemies to each other, who dispute about their Lord.” Surely, this was revealed concerning those people who came out from the ranks to fight on the day of Badr from the side of the Muslims: the chief of martyrs Sayyiduna Hamzah, Sayyiduna ‘Ali al-Murtada, and ‘Ubaidah bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with them), and from the side of the disbelievers: ‘Utbah and Shaybah, both sons of Rabi‘ah, and Walid bin ‘Utbah."
"2153","Az-Zuhri says: Sa'id bin al-Musayyib, 'Urwah bin al-Zubair, 'Alqamah bin Waqqas, and 'Ubaydullah bin 'Abdullah bin 'Utbah bin Mas'ud narrated to me this hadith from Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her), when those who accused her made their accusation and said what they said. Then Allah Almighty declared her innocent from their accusation. Az-Zuhri said: All of these people narrated to me a part of this hadith, and some of them remembered more of it than others, and were more precise and eloquent in their narration. I memorized from each what he narrated, and some parts of the narration confirm others. They stated that Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to travel, he would draw lots among his noble wives, and whichever woman's name was drawn, he would take her with him on the journey. Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drew lots during one of the journeys for jihad, and my name was drawn, so I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). This was after the command of hijab had been revealed. I would ride in my howdah, and when the caravan stopped, my howdah would be taken down. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the jihad and returned, and we were near Madinah, one night he gave the order to depart. When the people were informed of the departure, I stood up and walked until I was away from the army. When I finished my need and returned to my howdah, I touched my chest and realized that my necklace of Dhafar beads was missing (Dhafar is the name of a village in Yemen). I went back to look for the necklace, and searching for it delayed me. Meanwhile, the people who used to carry my howdah came, lifted it, and placed it on the camel I used to ride, thinking I was inside it. At that time, women were light (slender) because they ate little. So when they lifted the howdah and placed it on the camel, they did not notice its lightness. I was also a young girl. The people set off with the camel. I found my necklace after the whole army had left, and when I reached their camp, there was no sound or anyone to hear a sound. I decided to sit where I was, thinking that when they did not find me, they would return for me. While I was sitting there, sleep overcame me and I fell asleep. Safwan bin Mu'attal al-Sulami al-Dhakwani (may Allah be pleased with him), a man who used to stay behind the army at night for rest, came to my place in the morning. He noticed the body of a sleeping person, came to me, and recognized me as soon as he saw me, because he had seen me before the command of hijab was revealed. I woke up at his voice, and when he recognized me, he recited: ""Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un."" So I covered my face with my veil. By Allah! He did not speak to me, nor did I hear anything from him except ""Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un."" Then he made his camel kneel, placed his foot on its knee for me to mount, and I mounted the camel. He led the camel on foot until we reached the army, who had stopped in the heat of midday. So those who perished because of suspicion in my matter, perished, and the one about whom the Qur'an says ""tawalla kibrahu"" (he who took the lead in it), meaning the chief instigator of the accusation, was 'Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul (the leader of the hypocrites). Eventually, we arrived in Madinah, and when I reached Madinah, I fell ill and remained sick for a month. During that time, people were discussing the words of the slanderers, but I knew nothing of it. I only noticed that during my illness, I did not see the same kindness from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) as I used to see when I was sick before. During this period, he would only come in, greet me, and say, ""How are you?"" This made me suspicious, but I was unaware of the real issue, until after my illness, when I had become thin, I went out to Manasi' (a place outside Madinah), and with me was Umm Mistah. (Before toilets were built in people's houses, they would go out at night.) This was at a time when we did not have toilets in our houses, and we disliked building toilets near the house, as the earlier Arabs did. So I went out, and Umm Mistah was with me. She was the daughter of Abi Ruhm bin al-Muttalib bin 'Abd Manaf, and her mother was the daughter of Sakhr bin 'Amir, who was the maternal aunt of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) (her name was Salma). Her son's name was Mistah bin Athathah bin 'Ubad bin al-Muttalib. When we had finished our need and were returning home, Umm Mistah's foot got caught in her cloak and she said, ""May Mistah perish!"" I said, ""You have said a terrible thing! Do you abuse a man who was present at the Battle of Badr?"" She replied, ""O naive one! Have you not heard what Mistah has said?"" I said, ""What has he said?"" She told me what the slanderers had said. Upon hearing this, my illness increased. When I reached home, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came in, greeted me, and said, ""How are you?"" I said, ""Will you permit me to go to my parents?"" My intention was to confirm the news from my parents. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) gave me permission, and I went to my parents. I asked my mother, ""Mother! What are people saying?"" She said, ""My daughter, do not worry about it, and do not take it seriously. By Allah! It is rare for a man to have a beautiful wife whom he loves, and she has co-wives, but her co-wives do not find faults in her."" I said, ""Subhan Allah! Have people really started saying this?"" I wept all night, my tears did not stop, nor did I sleep, and I continued to weep in the morning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called 'Ali bin Abi Talib and Usamah bin Zayd, as no revelation had come down, and consulted them about separating from me (i.e., divorcing me). Usamah bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the opinion he knew about the Messenger of Allah's wife and her innocence, and his love for her. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! She is your wife, and we know nothing about her except good."" 'Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Allah has not put you in difficulty, and there are many women besides 'A'ishah. If you ask the slave-girl, she will tell you the truth."" (The slave-girl referred to is Barirah, who lived with 'A'ishah.) Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) called Barirah and asked, ""O Barirah! Have you ever seen anything in 'A'ishah that would make you doubt her chastity?"" Barirah replied, ""By Him Who sent you with the truth, if I had seen anything, I would have mentioned it. The only fault is that 'A'ishah is a young girl, she falls asleep and leaves the dough, and the goat comes and eats it."" (Meaning, she has no fault except that she is a naive young girl and, due to her youth, cannot manage the house.) Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood on the pulpit and sought an answer from 'Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul. He said on the pulpit, ""O Muslims! Who will help me against a man whose hurtful words have reached me concerning my family? By Allah! I know nothing but good of my wife ('A'ishah), and the man they accuse (Safwan bin Mu'attal), I know nothing but good of him, and he never entered my house except with me."" Upon hearing this, Sa'd bin Mu'adh al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), the chief of the Aws tribe, stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I will deal with him for you. If he is from our tribe, Aws, we will kill him, and if he is from our brothers, the Khazraj, command us and we will obey you."" Sa'd bin 'Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him), the chief of the Khazraj tribe and a good man, stood up, but at that moment, tribal zeal overtook him, and he said, ""By Allah! You are lying! You cannot kill a man from our tribe."" Then Usayd bin Hudayr, the cousin of Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him), stood up and said to Sa'd bin 'Ubadah, ""You are wrong! By Allah! We will kill him, and you are a hypocrite, defending the hypocrites."" The two tribes, Aws and Khazraj, stood up, and it was close to bloodshed, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was on the pulpit calming them down, until they became quiet and he also became quiet. Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I continued to weep all day, my tears did not stop, nor did I sleep, and my father thought my heart would break from weeping. My parents were sitting with me while I was crying. Then a woman from the Ansar asked permission to enter. I allowed her, and she sat down and began to weep with me. While we were in this state, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came in, greeted us, and sat down. Since the day the accusation was made against me, he had not sat with me, and a month had passed without any revelation regarding my case. Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sat down, he recited the tashahhud and said, ""As for what follows: O 'A'ishah, such-and-such has reached me about you. If you are innocent, Allah will soon declare your innocence, but if you have committed a sin, then repent and seek forgiveness from Allah, for when a servant confesses his sin and repents, Allah forgives him."" Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) finished his speech, my tears stopped completely, not a single drop remained. I said to my father, ""Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on my behalf."" He said, ""By Allah! I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" (Subhan Allah, her father was beloved to the Messenger of Allah, but in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, he could not speak, even though it was his daughter's case.) I said to my mother, ""Answer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on my behalf."" She said, ""By Allah! I do not know what to say to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" So I spoke myself, though I was a young girl and had not memorized much of the Qur'an. By Allah! I know that you have heard this story until it has settled in your hearts and you have believed it (and Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah said this out of anger, otherwise only the slanderers believed it). If I say I am innocent, and Allah knows I am innocent, you will not believe me. And if I admit to something I am innocent of, you will believe me. I find no example for myself and you except what the father of Yusuf (peace be upon him) said (she could not recall his name in her distress): ""So patience is most fitting, and Allah is the one sought for help against what you describe."" (Surah Yusuf) Then I turned away and lay down on my bed. By Allah! I knew I was innocent and that Allah would declare my innocence, but by Allah! I did not think that Qur'an would be revealed concerning me, which would be recited (until the Day of Judgment), for I did not consider myself worthy that Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, would speak about my case in His Book to be recited. I only hoped that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would see a dream in which Allah would declare my innocence. Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: By Allah! The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had not left his place, nor had anyone from the household gone out, when Allah revealed revelation to His Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and sent down Qur'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) felt the severity of the revelation, so much so that in the coldest of days, sweat would drip from his blessed body like pearls due to the weight of the words revealed to him (for it was the speech of the Supreme King). When this state passed (i.e., the revelation ended), the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled and the first words he spoke were: ""O 'A'ishah! Rejoice, for Allah has declared you innocent and pure."" My mother said, ""Get up and thank the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)."" I said, ""By Allah! I will not get up to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), nor will I praise anyone except Allah, for He is the One Who revealed my innocence."" Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Allah revealed: ""Indeed, those who brought forth the slander are a group among you. Do not think it bad for you; rather, it is good for you..."" until the end of ten verses, which Allah revealed for my innocence. Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), who used to spend on Mistah due to their close kinship and his poverty, said, ""By Allah! Now that he has said this about 'A'ishah, I will never give him anything."" Allah revealed the verse: ""Let not those among you who have virtue and wealth swear not to give to their relatives, the needy, and those who migrated for the sake of Allah. Do you not wish that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful."" Hibban bin Musa said that 'Abdullah bin Mubarak said: This verse is the greatest verse of hope in Allah's Book (because in it Allah promises forgiveness for maintaining ties of kinship). Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah! I wish that Allah should forgive me."" So he resumed giving Mistah what he used to give him and said, ""I will never stop."" Umm al-Mu'mineen 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also asked Umm al-Mu'mineen Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her) about me: ""What do you know or what have you seen?"" She replied (even though she was a co-wife), ""O Messenger of Allah! I guard my hearing and my sight (i.e., I do not say anything I have not heard or seen). I know nothing but good about 'A'ishah."" 'A'ishah al-Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her) was the only wife among the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) who could rival me, and Allah protected her from the accusation because of her piety. Her sister Hamnah bint Jahsh, however, supported her sister and fought for her, so she was among those who perished (i.e., participated in the slander). Az-Zuhri said: This is the final state of those people that has reached us."
"2154","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that people used to accuse a man regarding the Haram of the Prophet (i.e., the slave woman who was an umm walad of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Go and strike the neck of that man (perhaps he is a hypocrite or for some other reason deserving of death)."" Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) went to him and saw that he was bathing in a well to cool himself. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him, ""Come out."" He gave his hand to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who pulled him out and saw that his private part was cut off. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) did not kill him and came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! He is a majboob (i.e., his private part is cut off), he has no private part."" (So Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) understood that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had ordered his killing on suspicion of adultery, and for this reason he did not kill him. And perhaps the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had come to know through revelation that he would not be killed. But the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the order to kill him so that his condition would become apparent, and people would be ashamed of their accusation and their lie would be exposed.)"
"2155","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that Abdullah bin Ubayy bin Salul had two slave girls named Maseekah and Umaimah. He used to force both of them into prostitution. They complained about him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), then this verse was revealed: ""And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution if they desire chastity... Indeed, Allah is Most Forgiving, Most Merciful,"" up to the end."
"2156","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that some people from among the polytheists had committed much bloodshed and had committed much adultery while in the state of polytheism. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""What you say and the path to which you call is good, but tell us, is it an expiation for our past sins? (If it is an expiation, then we will accept Islam)."" Then this verse was revealed: ""Those who do not call upon any other god along with Allah, nor kill a soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery—and whoever does these (i.e., murder, adultery, and polytheism) shall meet a penalty. The punishment will be doubled for him on the Day of Resurrection, and he will abide therein in disgrace forever. Except for those who repent, believe, and do righteous deeds, for them Allah will replace their evil deeds with good, and Allah is Most Merciful, Most Forgiving."" (And Allah informed those people that if you accept Islam, all your previous sins from the time of polytheism will be forgiven.) And this verse was revealed: ""O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah..."" (the complete verse)."
"2157","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Allah Almighty says: I have prepared for My righteous servants that which no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never occurred to the heart of any human. All these blessings I have made ready. Leave aside what Allah has informed you (i.e., if the known blessings and pleasures are so excellent and good, then how wonderful will be the blessings and pleasures of Paradise about which Allah has not given any knowledge). Then he recited this verse: ""No one knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for their eyes"" (in Paradise)."
"2158","Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Allah Almighty's statement ""We will make them taste the lesser punishment..."" says that it refers to the hardships of this world, and (the incidents of) Rome and Batshah (or Dukhan). And Shu'bah is in doubt whether he said Batshah or Dukhan."
"2159","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: “When they came upon you from above you and from below you, and when the eyes shifted and the hearts reached the throats”—that this was revealed about the Battle of Khandaq (on that day, the Muslims faced extreme hardship. Allah Almighty said that We sent upon the disbelievers an army which you did not see, and a strong wind)."
"2160","`Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the saying of Allah, ""The sun runs on its fixed course,"" so he (peace be upon him) said: Its fixed place is beneath the Throne."
"2161","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that a Jewish scholar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, “O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Or O Abul Qasim (peace be upon him)! On the Day of Resurrection, Allah, the Exalted, will hold the heavens on one finger, the earths on one finger, the mountains and trees on one finger, the water and moist earth on one finger, and all creation on one finger. Then He will shake them and say, ‘I am the King, I am the King.’” Hearing this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled in amazement and affirmed the words of that scholar. Then he recited this verse: “They did not appraise Allah with true appraisal as is due to Him, and on the Day of Resurrection the whole earth will be in His grip, and the heavens will be rolled up in His right hand. Exalted is He and high above what they associate with Him.”"
"2162","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that three men gathered near the House of Allah; two of them were from the Quraysh and one from Thaqif, or two were from Thaqif and one from the Quraysh. Their understanding was little and their bellies were full of fat (from this it is understood that with obesity, wisdom is less). One of them said, ""What do you think, does Allah hear what we say?"" The second said, ""If we call out loudly, He will hear, and if we speak quietly, He will not hear."" The third said, ""If He hears when we call out loudly, then He will also hear when we speak quietly."" Then Allah revealed this verse: ""You did not conceal yourselves lest your ears, your eyes, and your skins would testify against you..."" (the whole verse: but you thought that many of the deeds you do, Allah does not know)."
"2163","Masruq says: We were sitting with Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) and he was lying down among us, when a man came and said, “O Abu Abdur Rahman! There is a storyteller at the gates of Kindah who says that the verse about smoke in the Qur’an refers to smoke that will come and suffocate the disbelievers, while the Muslims will only experience a cold-like sensation from it.” Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him) sat up angrily and said, “O people! Fear Allah. Whoever among you knows something should say it, and whoever does not know should say, ‘Allah knows best.’ For this is the essence of knowledge: that if one of you does not know something, he should say, ‘Allah knows best.’ Allah, Glorified and Exalted, said to His Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ‘Say, O Muhammad (peace be upon him), I do not ask you for any reward, nor am I one of those who pretend’ (__QUR_N__). When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saw the state of the people, that they would not accept through explanation, he said, ‘O Allah! Send upon them a seven-year famine like the seven years of famine during the time of Yusuf (peace be upon him).’ So a famine struck the Quraysh that consumed everything, until they ate skins and carrion out of hunger, and when one of them looked at the sky, it appeared to him like smoke. Then Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ‘O Muhammad (peace be upon him)! You command obedience to Allah and maintaining family ties, but your people have been destroyed. Pray to Allah for them.’ Allah the Exalted said, ‘So watch for the Day when the sky will bring a visible smoke, covering the people; this is a painful punishment...’ (__QUR_N__) until He said, ‘We will remove the punishment a little, but you will surely revert’ (__QUR_N__). If this verse referred to the punishment of the Hereafter, would it ever be removed? Then Allah the Exalted says, ‘On the Day We will strike with the greatest assault, We will surely take retribution’ (__QUR_N__). This ‘assault’ refers to the punishment at Badr, and these signs—smoke, the assault, the ‘lizam’, and the signs of Rome—have already passed.”"
"2164","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` five signs have already passed, and they are Dukhan, Lizam, Rome, Batshah, and Qamar (that is, the splitting of the moon)."
"2165","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that armed men from Makkah descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) from the mountain of Taneem. They intended to attack the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions by deception and in a state of heedlessness. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) captured them but did not kill them. Then Allah Almighty revealed this verse: ""That is, He is Allah who restrained their hands from you (and their deception did not succeed) and restrained your hands from them (that is, you did not kill them) after He had given you victory over them within the boundary of Makkah."
"2166","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When this verse was revealed, ""O you who believe! Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet... till the end,"" Sayyiduna Thabit bin Qais bin Shammas (may Allah be pleased with him) stayed in his house and said, ""I am among the people of Hell"" (because his voice was very loud and he was the orator of the Ansar, so he became afraid), and he stopped coming to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) asked Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him), ""O Abu Amr! What is the condition of Thabit? Has he fallen ill?"" Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""He is my neighbor, I do not know that he is ill."" Then Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) went to Sayyiduna Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) and conveyed to him what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had said. So Sayyiduna Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""This verse has been revealed, and you know that my voice is louder than the voice of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), (therefore) I am among the people of Hell."" Then Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) conveyed this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""No, rather he is among the people of Paradise."
"2167","‘Abdul Wahhab bin ‘Ata, regarding the statement of Allah ( ( The Day We will say to Hell... ) ) the verse, narrates from Sa‘id, who narrates from Qatadah, who narrates from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), who narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: People will continue to be thrown into Hell and it will keep saying, “Is there any more?” until Allah, the Mighty, will place His Foot in it. Then one part of it will draw back into another and it will say, “Enough, enough, by Your honor and generosity.” And there will remain space in Paradise until Allah creates a creation for it and places them in that space."
"2168","Abu Ishaq says: I saw a man who asked Aswad bin Yazid, and he used to teach the Qur'an in the mosque, ""Do you recite (muddakkir) with a dal or a dhal?"" He replied, ""I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) saying, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting (fahal min muddakkir) with a dal.'"" (That is, the letter without a dot.)"
"2169","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The angels were created from light, the jinn from a smokeless flame of fire, and our master Adam (peace be upon him) from that which has been described in the Qur’an (i.e., from clay)."
"2170","`Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` from the time we became Muslims until the revelation of this verse, ""Has the time not come for the hearts of those who believe to be humbled at the remembrance of Allah,"" for which Allah reproached us, four years had passed."
"2171","'Sayyiduna Urwah says that' Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said to me, ""O my nephew! People were commanded to seek forgiveness for the Companions, but instead they spoke ill of them."
"2172","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not recite the Qur'an to the jinn, nor did he see them. The fact is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went with his companions at that time to the market of 'Ukaz, when the doors of the heavens had been closed to the devils and flames of fire were being hurled at them. So a group of devils went back to their people and said, ""Our access to the heavens has been blocked and flames of fire are being thrown at us."" They said, ""There must be some new matter that is the cause of this, so go around to the east and west and find out what is the reason that the news from the heavens has stopped coming."" They began to roam the earth, turning to the east and west. Some of them came towards Tihamah (the land of Hijaz) to go to the market of 'Ukaz, and at that time the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was leading his companions in the Fajr prayer at (the place of) Nakhlah. When they heard the Qur'an, they listened attentively and said, ""This is the very reason the news from the heavens has ceased."" Then they returned to their people and said, ""O our people! We have heard a wondrous Qur'an which guides to the right path, so we have believed in it and we will never associate anyone with Allah."" Then Allah the Exalted revealed Surah al-Jinn to His Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Say (O Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him): It has been revealed to me that a group of jinn listened (to the Qur'an)."
"2173","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)` regarding Allah Almighty’s statement, “Do not move your tongue with it to hasten to remember it,” says that the incident is that at the time of the revelation of the Noble Qur’an, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would feel difficulty, so he would move his lips. Sa‘id said that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to me, “I move my lips for you as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to move his lips.” So Sa‘id said, “Just as Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas was moving his lips, I also move my lips in the same way.” Then Allah Almighty revealed this command: “Do not move your tongue to hasten to remember it. Indeed, upon Us is its collection and its recitation,” meaning, to gather it in your (peace and blessings be upon him) chest, so that you (peace and blessings be upon him) may recite it. (That is, at the time of the revelation of the revelation) you should listen silently and attentively, then its recitation is Our responsibility. After this divine command, when Jibril would bring the revelation, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would listen to his words in silence, and after his departure, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would repeat the same words that Jibril (peace be upon him) had said."
"2174","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) explained this verse, ""The Day when people will stand before the Lord of the worlds,"" by saying that some people will be standing, submerged in their sweat, which will reach up to the middle of their ears."
"2175","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever is called to account on the Day of Resurrection will be punished. I said: But Allah, the Exalted, says: “Then he will soon be given an easy reckoning, and he will return to his people rejoicing.” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: This is not the reckoning; this is only the presentation of deeds. Whoever is questioned in detail about the reckoning on the Day of Resurrection will be punished."
"2176","Sayyiduna Alqamah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We went to Syria, and Sayyiduna Abu Darda (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us and said, ""Is there anyone among you who recites according to the recitation of Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him)?"" I said, ""Yes! I am."" He said, ""How do you recite this verse: (By the night as it envelops)?"" I said, ""Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to recite it like this: (By the night as it envelops, and by the male and the female)."" He said, ""By Allah! I also heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recite it like this, and the people here want me to recite: (And by Him Who created the male and the female), but I do not accept their way."
"2177","Aswad bin Qais says: I heard from Sayyiduna Jundub bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) became ill and did not get up for two or three nights. Then a woman (A’warā bint Harb, the sister of Abu Sufyan, the wife of Abu Lahab, the carrier of firewood) came and said, “O Muhammad! I think your devil has left you (this she-devil said mockingly), because I see that he has not come to you for two or three nights.” Then Allah Almighty revealed this Surah: “By the morning brightness, and by the night when it covers with darkness, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor is He displeased.”"
"2178","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Shikhkhir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was reciting: “The mutual rivalry for piling up (worldly things) diverts you.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man says, “My wealth, my wealth,” but O man! What is your wealth? Your wealth is only that which you have eaten and consumed, or worn and worn out, or given in charity and sent ahead (for the Day of Resurrection)."
"2179","‘Sayyiduna Ubaidullah bin Utbah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said to me, “Do you know which is the last Surah to be revealed in its entirety in the Qur’an?” I said, “Yes! It is this Surah: ‘When the help of Allah comes and the victory comes.’” He said, “You have spoken the truth.”"
